---

<CaseStudy
  title="La Balma"
  subtitle="Another cooperative. Its own set of answers."
  heroPlaceholder="La Balma hero — gallery facade (photo needed)"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/gleis-21/', label: 'Gleis 21' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>La Balma is a 20-home cession-of-use cooperative promoted by Sostre Cívic in Barcelona’s Poblenou. Lacol and LaBoqueria designed the building with shared spaces distributed across its floors and circulation facing a public green corridor. <a class="source-link" href="https://lacol.coop/es/projectes/la-balma/">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>The project uses a base dwelling module with additional rooms managed through the cooperative, allowing different configurations. Shared spaces include guest, laundry and multipurpose rooms. The design describes passive strategies and centralized services; published design goals alone do not establish measured energy or cost outcomes.</p>
    <h2>A home can change without changing the address.</h2>
    <p>Rooms that can be reassigned as households grow or shrink are a compelling idea. The physical connection is only half the system: who gets an extra room, at what price, with what notice, and what happens when two households need it? Flexibility needs fair rules.</p>
    <p>Compare La Balma with La Borda for what changes, not just what repeats. The site, climate exposure, circulation and cooperative organization all shape the design. A repeatable process should carry lessons forward while leaving room for a different answer.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Test flexible layouts against accessibility, fire separation, acoustic privacy and fair allocation.</li>
<li>Put shared rooms on routes people use, while protecting quiet and personal space.</li>
<li>Share design and governance lessons, but price and model each new project independently.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://lacol.coop/es/projectes/la-balma/">Lacol · La Balma project account</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
